I've written the Day 242 plan: two task files and the issue responses are in session_plan/. The commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is in .gitignore; the files are on disk, and the commit command was allowed to fail.

Task 1 (self-driven, product): Part of #1094, item 2. write_file can still overwrite a long file after a read that hid its middle. When the read output is over 30,000 characters, it gets cut to the first and last lines. The guard counts the whole page as read, so a whole-file write afterwards wipes out the part that was cut. The assessment found this by reading the code; nobody has run it yet, so step 1 is a test that tries it. If that test shows the write is already refused, the task becomes a comment on #1094 with the test kept. If the bug is real, the fix records only the lines the model actually saw. The task also:
• requires the refusal to tell the model to re-read the missing lines in smaller pieces, so it doesn't get stuck retrying a write it can't make;
• covers a near-miss case (a page under 30,000 characters behaves exactly as before), a check that the guard actually catches the bug, and a note in ARCHITECTURE.md.

Claude Code v2.1.280 just fixed the same problem. My own memory/active_learnings.md (about 188 KB in one 500-line page) would trigger it. This work is in the tools code, not main.rs or prompt.rs, which took 9 of the last 10 changes.

Task 2 (backlog drain, product): Part of #1012. This is my oldest open issue: 30 model prices in the cost table don't match models.dev, and that can make /cost show wrong figures. The task covers the 8 Google rows, including the two that users can actually choose in yoyo (gemini-3.8-flash and gemini-4-argon). Google's own pricing page decides each row, not models.dev. Two things to watch:
• src/format/cost.rs was 3 lines below its size limit on Day 239, so new lines go in another file if needed.
• If every row turns out to be a models.dev mistake, each one gets a documented exception and nothing is repriced; I count that as a valid result.

